{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.UnitalGroebner.buchberger","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.buchberger","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.CompositionLemma"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.UnitalGroebner.buchberger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.buchberger","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/UnitalGroebner/buchberger.lean#L48-L76","doc":"**Buchberger's theorem — confluence consequence.**\n\nA Gröbner–Shirshov basis `sys` is confluent: whenever `f →* g₁` and\n`f →* g₂`, there is a common reduct `h` with `g₁ →* h` and\n`g₂ →* h`. This is the operational meaning of \"`G` is a GS basis for\n`I`\" — the division algorithm produces well-defined remainders.\n\nThe conclusion is a **concrete existential over `AlgElement`** (a\ncommon `MultiStepReduction` target), not a bare `Prop`. Proved from\n`confluence`.\nThe manuscript's standing hypothesis that the algebra has **no\nquasi-zeros** (Leitner–Pawloski; `monomial-basis.md`) is carried\nexplicitly as `hnqz`: it is what the S-polynomial half of the\ncomposition lemma needs, and it is discharged for the free algebra on\nany non-empty generating set by `noQuasiZerosFree_of_generator`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:buchberger","label":"thm:buchberger","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/buchberger.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}